turnip: say how much GPU memory each device holds.

Every graphics API Vessel runs reaches the GPU through Turnip -- DXVK, vkd3d
and Zink are all its Vulkan clients -- so a byte count here is the one VRAM
figure that covers D3D 8 to 12, OpenGL and Vulkan alike. DXVK's own allocator
figure covers D3D 8 to 11 only, vkd3d writes none, Zink none, and every KGSL
memory node is denied to apps.

Counted where a BO is really created (kgsl_bo_init, kgsl_bo_init_dmabuf) and
really destroyed (kgsl_bo_finish after the last reference). Published to
VESSEL_GPU_MEM_DIR/<pid>-<device> ("<bytes> <heap size>") from tu_queue_submit at most once a second,
only when it moved, via rename; removed in tu_DestroyDevice.

Motivation, measured: Empyrion crashed after six minutes at its main menu with
DxvkMemoryAllocator: Memory allocation failed, 6114 of 6136 MiB, and there was
no way to see how it got there.

